\nTo evaluate ${5}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2}={{5\\times 5}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=25\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429873 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1069 "q-64233" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1071 "${0}^{3}=$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1072 #uuid "c82d42be-b446-5866-87ca-88ea9428fb90" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429903 1074 "Here, ${0}^{3}$ is in exponent form. The base is $0$ and the exponent is $3.$ \n\nThis means that $0$ is taken as a factor $3$ times. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{0}^{3}={{0\\times 0\\times 0}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}=0.\n$$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429883 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1069 "q-224166" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1071 "What is the cube of $10?$\n\nThe cube of $10$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1072 #uuid "ca59627a-61c0-5ddb-824a-6032d58fc249" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429904 1074 "We need to evaluate ${10}^{3}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${10}^{3},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{10}^{3}={{10\\times 10\\times 10}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $10\\times 10=100,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{10\\times 10}_{⏟}}_{100}\\times 10 & =100\\times 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $100\\times 10=1,000,$ we have ${10}^{3}=1,000.$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429905 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429872 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429905 1069 "q-137627" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429905 1070 #edb/ref 1