] [17592186429907 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429907 1071 "What is the value of $9$ raised to the second power?\n\n$9$ raised to the second power is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429907 1072 #uuid "f30dc369-9201-5339-acfb-6423eb9240e9" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429907 1074 "We need to evaluate ${9}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${9}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{9}^{2}={{9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=81\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429876 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1069 "q-137617" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1071 "${9}^{3}=$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1072 #uuid "fdc760ae-ab2b-5525-82f1-1022c98537aa" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true] [17592186429908 1074 "To evaluate ${9}^{3},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{9}^{3}={{9\\times 9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $9\\times 9=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{81}\\times 9 & =81\\times 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $81\\times 9.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $81\\times 9=729,$ we have ${9}^{3}=729.$" 13194139534624 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00542389-ab01-5496-b4cb-a8421904c56d" 17592186429819 "answer-07edbe8b-8b99-5551-8907-2d61816753eb" 17592186429820 "answer-08e7a713-c709-